hadiths[21]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3684","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu': If a servant is sincere to his master and worships his Lord well, he will have his reward twice."
"3685","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, marfu': The shortest-lived of my Ummah is the one who reaches seventy."
"3686","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Which Hijrah is best?"" He said: ""That you abandon what Allah dislikes. And Hijrah is of two types: the Hijrah of the settled and the Hijrah of the nomad. As for the nomad, he obeys when commanded and responds when called. As for the settled, he has the greater trial and the superior reward."
"3687","[AI-translation] From Abu Mas'ud, he said: It was said to him, ""What did you hear the Messenger of Allah say concerning 'Za'amu' (they claimed)?"" He said: The Messenger of Allah said: ""A miserable mount for a man is 'Za'amu' (they claimed)."
"3688","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu': You hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from whoever hears from you."
"3689","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': The expiation for every quarrel is two rak'ahs."
"3690","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah from the Prophet, peace be upon him, he said: Three things I swear by: Allah does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share in it. The shares of Islam are three: fasting, prayer, and charity. Allah does not take a servant as a ward and then entrust him to another on the Day of Resurrection. A man does not love a people except that he comes with them on the Day of Resurrection. And the fourth, if I were to swear by it, I would not fear sinning: Allah does not cover a servant in this world except that He covers him in the Hereafter."
"3691","[AI-translation] From Muhammad bin Sa'd from his father, marfu': Three things are of happiness and three are of misery. As for happiness: a wife whom you find pleasing and when absent you trust her concerning herself and your wealth, a mount that is gentle-paced so it catches you up with your companions, and a house that is spacious with many amenities. As for misery: a wife whom you see and she displeases you, and she attacks you with her tongue, and if you are absent you do not trust her concerning herself and your wealth, a mount that is sluggish, for if you beat it, it tires you, and if you leave it, it does not catch you up with your companions, and a house that is narrow with few amenities."
"3692","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': The maternal uncle is an heir."
"3693","[AI-translation] From 'Awf bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, he said: Dreams are of three types: among them are terrifying dreams from Satan to grieve the son of Adam; among them is what a man thinks about during his waking hours, so he sees it in his sleep; and among them is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3694","[AI-translation] From 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! When you dispatch me, shall I be like a heated branding iron, or does the witness see what the absent one does not see? He said: The witness sees what the absent one does not see."
"3695","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu'an: The slave, when he is sincere to his master and excels in the worship of Allah, for him is his reward twice."
"3696","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu'an: The slave, when he is sincere to his master and excels in the worship of Allah, for him is his reward twice."
"3697","[AI-translation] Nabighah that he had two wives: a Lihyaniyyah and a Mu'awiyyah from the Banu Mu'awiyah ibn Zayd. They met and became jealous, so the Mu'awiyyah picked up a stone and threw it at the Lihyaniyyah while she was pregnant and had reached full term. She killed her and she delivered a boy. Hamal ibn Malik said to 'Imran ibn 'Uwaymir: Pay me the blood money for my wife. They presented themselves to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he said: The blood money is upon the 'Asabah, and for the miscarriage is the price of a male or female slave."
"3698","[AI-translation] From 'Amr ibn Hazm: Intentional killing is retaliation, and accidental killing is blood money."
"3699","[AI-translation] From 'Umar, marfu'an: For the nose, if its cutting is complete, the blood money is one hundred camels. For the hand, fifty; for the foot, fifty; for the head wound (ammah), one-third of the blood money; for the penetrating wound (ja'ifah), one-third of the blood money; for the skull fracture (munaqqilah), fifteen; for the bone-exposing wound (mudihah), five; for the tooth, five; and for each finger from among those, ten."
"3700","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: For the righteous enslaved slave are two rewards. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, were it not for jihad in the cause of Allah, and Hajj, and kindness to my mother, I would have loved to die while I was a slave."
"3701","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: Whoever helps his brother in his absence, Allah helps him in this world and the Hereafter."
"3702","[AI-translation] Sadusi who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! or he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! If you were to commit sins until your sins filled what is between the heaven and the earth, then you sought forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He would forgive you. And by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! or: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! If you did not commit sins, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would bring a people who commit sins, then seek forgiveness from Allah, and He would forgive them."
"3703","[AI-translation] From Nafi' that 'Umar dispatched an army and appointed a man called Sariyah over them. While 'Umar was delivering the sermon on Friday, he said: O Sariyah! The mountain! O Sariyah! The mountain! They found Sariyah had moved towards the mountain at that very hour on Friday, and between them was a month's journey."
"3704","[AI-translation] From Aishah, marfu'an: ""O Aishah! Your people are the fastest of my Ummah to catch up with me."" She said: ""So when he sat down, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! May Allah make me your ransom! You entered saying words that startled me.' He said: 'And what is it?' She said: 'You claim that my people are the fastest of your Ummah to catch up with you.' He said: 'Yes.' She said: 'And why is that?' He said: 'Deaths are made sweet for them, and their Ummah envies them.' She said: 'So I said: And how will the people be after that, or at that time?' He said: 'Like locusts, whose strong eat their weak, until the Hour is established upon them.'"
